KZ3 patch 1144 (SPU pass 129), switch KZ3_WAITSTAT=1 (default off: no prints, no clock reads): "[waitstat]" counters on every timed host wait that goes through Wine's RtlWaitOnAddress
(SleepConditionVariable* with a finite timeout): lv2s_sleep (the live sys_lwmutex/lwcond/mutex/cond core, patch 1122),
sys_event_queue_receive and sys_event_flag_wait, spu_channels ch_wait (10 ms), spu_workload WAIT_SIGNAL (1 s), the
lv2_register SPU-port bind wait, cellSpurs ef_wait_timed, cellSync2 cond/queue waits, the sysPrxForUser lwcond HLE.
lv2s_sleep also records how close each timeout lies to the last wake of the same mutex (near2us / near20us / near100us / near1ms),
the upper bound of the Wine race exposure. Diagnostic only, behaviour unchanged (GetLastError is read before the note).
Decides which site a fix patch has to cover.

